    "body": "### Problem\n\nHi all,\n\nFirst time trying to build this from source so forgive me if this is known. I wanted to try out a build without Unibilium. The BUILD.md file says:\n\n> To confirm at runtime that unibilium was not included, check `has('terminfo') == 1`.\n\nWhen I follow the instructions and build it, however, I get `0` from `:echo has('terminfo')`.\n\nI am on WSL with Ubuntu 24.04.4. The command I used to build neovim was:\n`make CMAKE_EXTRA_FLAGS=\"-DENABLE_UNIBILIUM=0\" DEPS_CMAKE_FLAGS=\"-DUSE_BUNDLED_UNIBILIUM=0\" CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo`\nI am on the `nightly` tag, which currently points to commit `187d13aa6047e1914244e8033b2d2f3379a0b97f`.\n\nI don't believe that this version *was* built with unibilium, since I don't see it in the cmake output like I do when I exclude the unibillium-disabling flags. Nonetheless `has('terminfo')` returns `0`. \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `git checkout nightly`\n2. `make CMAKE_EXTRA_FLAGS=\"-DENABLE_UNIBILIUM=0\" DEPS_CMAKE_FLAGS=\"-DUSE_BUNDLED_UNIBILIUM=0\" CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo`\n3. run the new `nvim` build, `build/bin/nvim --clean` (no extra plugins necessary)\n4. Within Neovim, `:echo has('terminfo')`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nI expect `:echo has('terminfo')` to be `1`.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1952+g187d13aa60\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nI don't think Vim even has this otion\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nWSL (Ubuntu 24.04.4)\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nWindows Terminal 1.24.12741.0\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
